IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa25-valuation.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 37, "Requirements as to independent valuation":
-- ss 1149 to 1153 (lines 16341-16409 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; NOTES.md, "Reading a result").
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words: -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide: -- NOTHING-kind (<why>), <why> being one of: silent, list not closed,
--               includes, undefined term, points outside the text, limited by its own wording.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Answers other parts give are INPUTS under the names PLAN.md section 4 gives them (s 1212, s 1162, s 1121).
-- Every name below begins with the section label it implements.

§ `Part 37: companies, supplementary provisions`

§§ `Requirements as to independent valuation`

-- ---- s 1149: Application of valuation requirements -----------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1149 provision requiring the valuation and report` IS ONE OF
    `s 1149 s 93 (re-registration as public company: recent allotment of shares for non-cash consideration)`
    `s 1149 s 593 (allotment of shares of public company in consideration of non-cash asset)`
    `s 1149 s 599 (transfer of non-cash asset to public company)`
    `s 1149 another provision`

-- src:16342 | 1149 Application of valuation requirements
-- src:16343 | The provisions of sections 1150 to 1153 apply to the valuation and report required by—
-- src:16344 | section 93 (re-registration as public company: recent allotment of shares for non-cash consideration);
-- src:16345 | section 593 (allotment of shares of public company in consideration of non-cash asset);
-- src:16346 | section 599 (transfer of non-cash asset to public company).
@ref s 1149 Application of valuation requirements (src:16342-16346)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 1149 provision requiring the valuation and report`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1149 sections 1150 to 1153 apply to the valuation and report` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `s 1149 another provision` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the three provisions are listed without "only"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 1150: Valuation by qualified independent person -------------------------------------------------

-- src:16347 | 1150 Valuation by qualified independent person
-- src:16348 | (1) The valuation and report must be made by a person (“the valuer”) who—
-- src:16349 | (a) is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor (see section 1212), and
-- src:16350 | (b) meets the independence requirement in section 1151.
@ref s 1150(1) The valuer (src:16347-16350)
GIVEN `s 1212 the person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1151 the person meets the independence requirement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1150(1) the person may make the valuation and report` MEANS
    IF `s 1212 the person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The valuation and report must be made by a person (“the valuer”) who— (a) is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor" (a bare "must" not met: decided at this site, fork F5)
    ELSE IF `s 1151 the person meets the independence requirement` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The valuation and report must be made by a person (“the valuer”) who— (b) meets the independence requirement in section 1151" (a bare "must" not met: decided at this site, fork F5)
         ELSE IF `s 1212 the person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 1151 the person meets the independence requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1212 or s 1151 is not known

-- Subsection (3): "The references in subsection (2)(b) to an officer or employee do not include an auditor."
-- src:16358 | (3) The references in subsection (2)(b) to an officer or employee do not include an auditor.
@ref s 1150(3) An auditor is not an officer or employee for subsection (2)(b) (src:16358)
GIVEN `the person is an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1150(3) the person counts as an officer or employee for subsection (2)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the person is an auditor`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The references in subsection (2)(b) to an officer or employee do not include an auditor"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (3) says nothing of a person who is not an auditor

-- The other person may be arranged for, or accepted, only if (a) and (b) hold. Limb (b) asks whether that person is an
-- officer or employee of the company or of a related body corporate (or a partner of, or employed by, one): the input
-- counts only a person who is NOT an auditor, as subsection (3) requires.
-- src:16351 | (2) However, where it appears to the valuer to be reasonable for the valuation of the consideration, or part of it, to be made by (or for him to accept a valuation made by) another person who—
-- src:16352 | (a) appears to him to have the requisite knowledge and experience to value the consideration or that part of it, and
-- src:16353 | (b) is not an officer or employee of—
-- src:16354 | (i) the company, or
-- src:16355 | (ii) any other body corporate that is that company's subsidiary or holding company or a subsidiary of that company's holding company,
-- src:16356 | or a partner of or employed by any such officer or employee,
-- src:16357 | he may arrange for or accept such a valuation, together with a report which will enable him to make his own report under this section.
@ref s 1150(2) Another person may make the valuation (src:16351-16357)
GIVEN `it appears to the valuer to be reasonable for the valuation, or part of it, to be made by (or for him to accept a valuation made by) the other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the valuer that the other person has the requisite knowledge and experience to value the consideration or that part of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is an officer or employee, other than an auditor, of the company or of a subsidiary or holding company of it or a subsidiary of its holding company, or a partner of or employed by such an officer or employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1150(2) the valuer may arrange for or accept a valuation made by the other person` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the valuer to be reasonable for the valuation, or part of it, to be made by (or for him to accept a valuation made by) the other person`
       AND `it appears to the valuer that the other person has the requisite knowledge and experience to value the consideration or that part of it`
       AND NOT `the other person is an officer or employee, other than an auditor, of the company or of a subsidiary or holding company of it or a subsidiary of its holding company, or a partner of or employed by such an officer or employee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "However, where it appears to the valuer to be reasonable ... another person who— (a) appears to him to have the requisite knowledge and experience ..., and (b) is not an officer or employee of— (i) the company, or (ii) any other body corporate ..." (a grant of power limited by its own wording)

-- Subsection (4): where another person values, the valuer's report must say so and state and describe what follows.
-- src:16359 | (4) Where the consideration or part of it is valued by a person other than the valuer himself, the latter's report must state that fact and shall also—
-- src:16360 | (a) state the former's name and what knowledge and experience he has to carry out the valuation, and
-- src:16361 | (b) describe so much of the consideration as was valued by the other person, and the method used to value it, and specify the date of that valuation.
@ref s 1150(4) The valuer's report where another person values (src:16359-16361)
GIVEN `the consideration or part of it is valued by a person other than the valuer himself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1150(4) the requirement as to the valuer's report applies` MEANS
    IF `the consideration or part of it is valued by a person other than the valuer himself`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the consideration or part of it is valued by a person other than the valuer himself" (a "where" that fails: the 2026-11-05 ruling)

-- src:16359 | (4) Where the consideration or part of it is valued by a person other than the valuer himself, the latter's report must state that fact and shall also—
-- src:16360 | (a) state the former's name and what knowledge and experience he has to carry out the valuation, and
-- src:16361 | (b) describe so much of the consideration as was valued by the other person, and the method used to value it, and specify the date of that valuation.
@ref s 1150(4) The valuer's report where another person values (src:16359-16361)
GIVEN `the consideration or part of it is valued by a person other than the valuer himself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states that fact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states the other person's name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states what knowledge and experience the other person has to carry out the valuation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report describes so much of the consideration as was valued by the other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report describes the method used to value it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report specifies the date of that valuation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1150(4) the valuer's report contains what is required` MEANS
    IF NOT `the consideration or part of it is valued by a person other than the valuer himself`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the requirement does not engage, so nothing is left to fail (fork F5)
    ELSE IF `the report states that fact`
            AND `the report states the other person's name`
            AND `the report states what knowledge and experience the other person has to carry out the valuation`
            AND `the report describes so much of the consideration as was valued by the other person`
            AND `the report describes the method used to value it`
            AND `the report specifies the date of that valuation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the latter's report must state that fact and shall also— (a) state the former's name and what knowledge and experience he has to carry out the valuation, and (b) describe so much of the consideration as was valued by the other person, and the method used to value it, and specify the date of that valuation" (a bare "must" not done: decided at this site, fork F5)

DECLARE `s 1150 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 1150 the valuer`
    `s 1153 an officer of the company`

DECLARE `s 1150 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 1150 state in the report that another person valued the consideration, and give that person's name, knowledge and experience, what was valued, the method and the date`

-- src:16359 | (4) Where the consideration or part of it is valued by a person other than the valuer himself, the latter's report must state that fact and shall also—
-- src:16360 | (a) state the former's name and what knowledge and experience he has to carry out the valuation, and
-- src:16361 | (b) describe so much of the consideration as was valued by the other person, and the method used to value it, and specify the date of that valuation.
@ref s 1150(4) The valuer's report where another person values (src:16359-16361)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 1150 party` `s 1150 act`
`s 1150(4) the valuer must state in the report what is required` MEANS
    PARTY `s 1150 the valuer`
    MUST `s 1150 state in the report that another person valued the consideration, and give that person's name, knowledge and experience, what was valued, the method and the date`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 1150 the valuer` BECAUSE "s 1150(4): the report does not state the required particulars of the valuation made by another person"

-- ---- s 1151: The independence requirement -------------------------------------------------------------

-- "only if": read as the complete test (fork F8). Each input is the fact the person would state, put as the
-- disqualifying fact; an auditor of the company is not counted as an officer or employee (subsection (2)).
-- src:16362 | 1151 The independence requirement
-- src:16363 | (1) A person meets the independence requirement for the purposes of section 1150 only if—
-- src:16364 | (a) he is not—
-- src:16365 | (i) an officer or employee of the company, or
-- src:16366 | (ii) a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner;
-- src:16367 | (b) he is not—
-- src:16368 | (i) an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of the company, or
-- src:16369 | (ii) a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner; and
-- src:16370 | (c) there does not exist between—
-- src:16371 | (i) the person or an associate of his, and
-- src:16372 | (ii) the company or an associated undertaking of the company,
-- src:16373 | a connection of any such description as may be specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 1151(1) The independence requirement (src:16362-16373)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or employee of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a partner or employee of such an officer or employee of an associated undertaking, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a connection of a description specified by regulations exists between the person or an associate of his and the company or an associated undertaking of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1151(1) the person meets the independence requirement` MEANS
    IF `the person is an officer or employee of the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person meets the independence requirement for the purposes of section 1150 only if— (a) he is not— (i) an officer or employee of the company"
    ELSE IF `the person is a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) he is not— ... (ii) a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner"
         ELSE IF `the person is an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of the company`
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) he is not— (i) an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of the company"
              ELSE IF `the person is a partner or employee of such an officer or employee of an associated undertaking, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner`
                   THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) he is not— ... (ii) a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner"
                   ELSE IF `a connection of a description specified by regulations exists between the person or an associate of his and the company or an associated undertaking of the company`
                        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) there does not exist between— (i) the person or an associate of his, and (ii) the company or an associated undertaking of the company, a connection of any such description as may be specified by regulations"
                        ELSE JUST TRUE -- every limb of "only if" is met: read as the complete test (fork F8)

-- src:16374 | (2) An auditor of the company is not regarded as an officer or employee of the company for this purpose.
@ref s 1151(2) An auditor of the company is not regarded as an officer or employee of the company (src:16374)
GIVEN `the person is an auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1151(2) the person is regarded as an officer or employee of the company for the independence requirement` MEANS
    IF `the person is an auditor of the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An auditor of the company is not regarded as an officer or employee of the company for this purpose"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) says nothing of a person who is not an auditor

-- src:16375 | (3) In this section—
-- src:16376 | “associated undertaking” means—
-- src:16377 | (a) a parent undertaking or subsidiary undertaking of the company, or
-- src:16378 | (b) a subsidiary undertaking of a parent undertaking of the company; and
-- src:16379 | “associate” has the meaning given by section 1152.
@ref s 1151(3) "Associated undertaking" (src:16375-16379)
GIVEN `s 1162 the undertaking is a parent undertaking of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1162 the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1162 the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of a parent undertaking of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1151(3) the undertaking is an associated undertaking of the company` MEANS
    IF `s 1162 the undertaking is a parent undertaking of the company`
       OR `s 1162 the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of the company`
       OR `s 1162 the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of a parent undertaking of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“associated undertaking” means— (a) a parent undertaking or subsidiary undertaking of the company, or (b) a subsidiary undertaking of a parent undertaking of the company"

-- ---- s 1152: Meaning of "associate" -------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Subsection (1) says what the section is for (inert, reason 1: fork F2). In each definition below the text says what
-- "associate" "means": the list is closed. Subsection (6): for a limited liability partnership, "director" reads
-- "member", so a limited liability partnership of which the person is a member takes the place of a body corporate
-- of which the person is a director.

DECLARE `s 1152 relationship of the other person to the individual` IS ONE OF
    `s 1152 the individual's spouse or civil partner or minor child or step-child`
    `s 1152 a body corporate of which the individual is a director`
    `s 1152 a limited liability partnership of which the individual is a member`
    `s 1152 an employee or partner of the individual`
    `s 1152 none of these relationships to the individual`

-- src:16383 | (2) In relation to an individual, “associate” means—
-- src:16384 | (a) that individual's spouse or civil partner or minor child or step-child,
-- src:16385 | (b) any body corporate of which that individual is a director, and
-- src:16386 | (c) any employee or partner of that individual.
@ref s 1152(2) Associate of an individual (src:16383-16386)
GIVEN relationship IS A `s 1152 relationship of the other person to the individual`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1152(2) the other person is an associate of the individual` MEANS
    CONSIDER relationship
    WHEN `s 1152 none of these relationships to the individual` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to an individual, “associate” means— (a) that individual's spouse or civil partner or minor child or step-child, (b) any body corporate of which that individual is a director, and (c) any employee or partner of that individual"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 1152 relationship of the other person to the body corporate` IS ONE OF
    `s 1152 a body corporate of which the body is a director`
    `s 1152 a limited liability partnership of which the body is a member`
    `s 1152 a body corporate in the same group as the body`
    `s 1152 an employee or partner of the body or of a body corporate in the same group`
    `s 1152 none of these relationships to the body corporate`

-- src:16387 | (3) In relation to a body corporate, “associate” means—
-- src:16388 | (a) any body corporate of which that body is a director,
-- src:16389 | (b) any body corporate in the same group as that body, and
-- src:16390 | (c) any employee or partner of that body or of any body corporate in the same group.
@ref s 1152(3) Associate of a body corporate (src:16387-16390)
GIVEN relationship IS A `s 1152 relationship of the other person to the body corporate`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1152(3) the other person is an associate of the body corporate` MEANS
    CONSIDER relationship
    WHEN `s 1152 none of these relationships to the body corporate` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to a body corporate, “associate” means— (a) any body corporate of which that body is a director, (b) any body corporate in the same group as that body, and (c) any employee or partner of that body or of any body corporate in the same group"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 1152 relationship of the other person to the partnership that is a legal person` IS ONE OF
    `s 1152 a body corporate of which the partnership is a director`
    `s 1152 a limited liability partnership of which the partnership is a member`
    `s 1152 an employee of or partner in the partnership`
    `s 1152 a person who is an associate of a partner in the partnership`
    `s 1152 none of these relationships to the partnership`

-- src:16391 | (4) In relation to a partnership that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed, “associate” means—
-- src:16392 | (a) any body corporate of which that partnership is a director,
-- src:16393 | (b) any employee of or partner in that partnership, and
-- src:16394 | (c) any person who is an associate of a partner in that partnership.
@ref s 1152(4) Associate of a partnership that is a legal person (src:16391-16394)
GIVEN relationship IS A `s 1152 relationship of the other person to the partnership that is a legal person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1152(4) the other person is an associate of the partnership that is a legal person` MEANS
    CONSIDER relationship
    WHEN `s 1152 none of these relationships to the partnership` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to a partnership that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed, “associate” means— (a) any body corporate of which that partnership is a director, (b) any employee of or partner in that partnership, and (c) any person who is an associate of a partner in that partnership"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16395 | (5) In relation to a partnership that is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed, “associate” means any person who is an associate of any of the partners.
@ref s 1152(5) Associate of a partnership that is not a legal person (src:16395)
GIVEN `the other person is an associate of any of the partners` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1152(5) the other person is an associate of the partnership that is not a legal person` MEANS
    IF `the other person is an associate of any of the partners`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to a partnership that is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed, “associate” means any person who is an associate of any of the partners"

-- ---- s 1153: Valuer entitled to full disclosure ------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16397 | 1153 Valuer entitled to full disclosure
-- src:16398 | (1) A person carrying out a valuation or making a report with respect to any consideration proposed to be accepted or given by a company, is entitled to require from the officers of the company such information and explanation as he thinks necessary to enable him to—
-- src:16399 | (a) carry out the valuation or make the report, and
-- src:16400 | (b) provide any note required by section 596(3) or 600(3) (note required where valuation carried out by another person).
@ref s 1153(1) The valuer's entitlement to information and explanation from the officers (src:16397-16400)
GIVEN `the person is carrying out a valuation or making a report with respect to consideration proposed to be accepted or given by a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information and explanation is such as the person thinks necessary to carry out the valuation or make the report, or to provide a note required by section 596(3) or 600(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1153(1) the person is entitled to require the information and explanation from the officers of the company` MEANS
    IF `the person is carrying out a valuation or making a report with respect to consideration proposed to be accepted or given by a company`
       AND `the information and explanation is such as the person thinks necessary to carry out the valuation or make the report, or to provide a note required by section 596(3) or 600(3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is entitled to require from the officers of the company such information and explanation as he thinks necessary to enable him to— (a) carry out the valuation or make the report, and (b) provide any note required by section 596(3) or 600(3)"

-- src:16402 | (3) Subsection (2) applies to a statement—
-- src:16403 | (a) made (whether orally or in writing) to a person carrying out a valuation or making a report, and
-- src:16404 | (b) conveying or purporting to convey any information or explanation which that person requires, or is entitled to require, under subsection (1).
@ref s 1153(3) The statement to which subsection (2) applies (src:16402-16404)
GIVEN `the statement is made (whether orally or in writing) to a person carrying out a valuation or making a report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement conveys or purports to convey information or explanation which that person requires, or is entitled to require, under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1153(3) the statement is one to which subsection (2) applies` MEANS
    IF `the statement is made (whether orally or in writing) to a person carrying out a valuation or making a report`
       AND `the statement conveys or purports to convey information or explanation which that person requires, or is entitled to require, under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (2) applies to a statement— (a) made (whether orally or in writing) to a person carrying out a valuation or making a report, and (b) conveying or purporting to convey any information or explanation which that person requires, or is entitled to require, under subsection (1)" (a scope limit with no "only": the 2026-11-05 ruling)

-- src:16401 | (2) A person who knowingly or recklessly makes a statement to which this subsection applies that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular commits an offence.
@ref s 1153(2) Offence of making a misleading, false or deceptive statement to a valuer (src:16401)
GIVEN `the person makes the statement knowingly or recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1153(3) the statement is one to which subsection (2) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1153(2) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1153(3) the statement is one to which subsection (2) applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the person makes the statement knowingly or recklessly` AND `the statement is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who knowingly or recklessly makes a statement ... that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular commits an offence"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a statement to which this subsection applies"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a statement to which this subsection applies" (the s 1153(3) answer is NOTHING)

-- src:16405 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (2) is liable—
-- src:16406 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:16407 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:16408 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:16409 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 1153(4) Penalty for an offence under s 1153(2) (src:16405-16409)
GIVEN `how convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
      guilty IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1153(4) the penalty for an offence under s 1153(2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER guilty
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `how convicted`
        WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN
            JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
                               `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 2, unit IS Years)
                               `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
                               `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
                               `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
